# Raw observed output — the two MPD panels get independent switches (2026-10-13, win32)

## The defect
packages/mpd-tui-plugin/src/index.ts:  `enabled: resolved.panel`  (the MPD page)
packages/mpd-tui-plugin/src/index.ts:  `enabled: resolved.panel`  (the workmate page too — the SAME knob)
packages/mpd-tui-plugin/src/panel-workmate.ts: "…disabled by the mpd-tui row config (panel: false)"
=> the two pages could not be toggled apart.

## The fix
Config (row-config type + schema):  panel?: boolean   +   workmate?: boolean  (default true)
resolveConfig:                      panel: bool(config.panel, true)
                                    workmate: bool(config.workmate, true)
registration:                       MPD page -> resolved.panel        workmate page -> resolved.workmate
panel-workmate.ts message:          "…(workmate: false)"

## Typecheck caught a REAL omission (and then passed)
$ bun run typecheck
packages/mpd-tui-plugin/src/index.ts(222,27): error TS2339: Property 'workmate' does not exist on type 'Config'.
packages/mpd-tui-plugin/test/plugin.test.ts(339,7): error TS2769: No overload matches this call.
packages/mpd-tui-plugin/test/plugin.test.ts(996,72): error TS2353: 'workmate' does not exist in type 'Config'
FIX: added `workmate?: boolean` to the exported Config interface.
$ bun run typecheck   -> tsgo --noEmit, exit 0

## The two arms (the independence is FALSIFIABLE, not decorative)
$ bun test packages/mpd-tui-plugin -t "with the MPD panel off"
(pass) … > with the MPD panel off, only that page is skipped and both entry points keep the scene path [84.30ms]
 1 pass / 0 fail
$ bun test packages/mpd-tui-plugin -t "with the WORKMATE panel off"
(pass) … > with the WORKMATE panel off, only that page is skipped — the MPD page stays [87.60ms]
 1 pass / 0 fail

